{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "dd5045e6b3ee47398424c170ba253771",
    "m_Title": "Solve Waves",
    "m_Content": "This function adds a bit of dynamic interaction for the liquid with the game world. It enabled you to pass a Vector4 array from C# which defines waves (like impact splashes or wakes from the player). The B2URuntimeUtility object allows you to instantiate a wave into a specific mesh. The Vector4 array stores the position, as well as a packed value in W. In the packed value it writes a temporary 8 bit mesh ID to the wave to prevent ripples from one separated body of liquid from another. It also stores the amplitude of the wave, and the wave time. The utility also writes a matching 8 bit mesh ID to the RSUV of the mesh so that for a wave to be evaluated, it must match the mesh ID and wave ID. Using these values along side the viscosity of the liquid, we can create dynamic ripples in the water that propagate outward and even interfere with each other if multiple hit nearby. ",
    "m_TextSize": 0,
    "m_Theme": 0,
